cml14rk0h00047obq3ryvrhqa	cml14qzjq00037obqulgcbqr1	Chapter 1	Oliver watson sat in his ????? listening to Mozart's requiem. He'd been humming along since leaving the station, oblivious to the new trainee sitting next to him. Not a word said between them. Oliver was wondering to himself “ is he the timmid type, or the hidden gifts type”. He glanced across as the music came out of one of its dark patches.  The music changed into light summery piqueting music, letting go of his emotions as they bounced from cloud to cloud, the crechendo was coming up, but not yet there was still a while for it to build up.\n“You're not from around here then”? He asked speaking loudly to get through the violins that were starting the build up. With a glance to his side he wanted to see sam's face, he'd been introduced to him the previous evening and that he would assist him. It had got his goat at first, his assistant, as if he needed an assistant to crack cases. \nHis first opinion about him came when he'd tried to crack the same old joke, “so where was sherlock”, the chief Gaberati who was introducing them had heard it before and to Olivers grateful look, looked at sam with  bored eyes and continued his Introduction. Same as you, from hertfordshire originally, you should get along” he looked at Oliver with a new look, one of authority , the strongest inferance he'd had yet in his 5 years situated in the north, as a command to him. He decided to challenge, he had no boss, though deep down, he'd taken a real liking to him “what you trying to say, I don't get on with people”. This time he got a “don't take the piss” look. He knew he'd been quite gruff with people here, it had taken a while since he'd got there from London to the relaxed pace of things and to actually relax. The weather controlled everything. The farmers to the tourists, the main group of people there at any one time. Crimes outside the main town of windermere were thefts, personal disputes between couples or between friends, deaths were time consuming seeing as they had to investigate, and there were a large number of retired people in the area refusing to go into homes, (living as they always had and refusing till their dying breath to change their habits) he'd remarqued that as something he'd admired when he'd first seen it. Since then, it had become more a question when he'd seen the state some of them lived in in their old delapidted farms, why the fuck not move to a home, he knew he'd be more comfortable in a home when the time came, regular food, soft bed and most importantly, warmth. The cold in the houses he'd visited in winter, he'd, wondered how people could live with just a fire burning, small room's admitedly, but with gales still blowing through the windows and under the doors.\n“no, originated from near where you originated”. “Piece of advice, Don't get cocky wi me son and we'lll get on well, what town d'ya go to school”, he heard it as it came out, probably the influence from sam. He'd stopped pronouncing his words correctly as he'd learned to try and hide his accent. He'd tried speaking correctly, the queens english, he felt it had given him more authority than the grief he'd gotten when his southern accent came out, he'd spent his first year in the north in Edinburgh. There the accent was (so he'd been told) as close to the queens english as you'd get. It had the slight lilt of the scottish accent but everything sounded correct and completely comprehensible.\nHe'd listened and almost studied their words and sentences till he felt he'd lost the edge and his accent was now camoflaged. He didn't like standing out here, on his home turf back a few years, it had been a diferrent story, He'd earned commendations, been the first in the fray, eager to serve, commited. Things had changed when is wife died, they had no children, and it had been a particularly brutal gangland murder case that had ended it for him, 4 men found in a car in the middle of winter in a forest in essex, 4 vicous gangland members that had been put out of circulation. The threats that had flown around after, he being a reciever as he had had to be quite heavy handed to get out the hat could be the truth, there was still conspiracy theories flying around about it. He had still been getting over the anger of his wifes death, it had worn him out. “Early retirement or a posting somewhere out of harms way” were the words his boss had used.\n“Broxbourne, near enfield” he heard. “I know it, from Hertford mesel”.\nHe heard his slip again and promised himself to take more care.\n““what's the call” he followed\n“Body found by lake ????????, no identification, nothing in his pockets, no idea where, who it was or where he had come from”, Oliver nodded. They were almost there. The music was getting there, he slowed down going through the winding lanes with moss covered stone walls still leaved, drapping fruitess bramble branches.\nThe final days of summer were past and autumn was hitting with cold mornings and mist in the dull green and yellow grass dotting the sides of the rocky mountains around and in their valleys. The music lifted and he had a sudden urge to open the window, to amplify the music and feel it echoing around the valley, the thought of the cold blast smacking in through the window quickly sent a shiver down his spine and the idea went with it.\nHe saw the blue flashing somewhere ahead and he knew they were near. He looked up and dark clouds had appeared above the cragy ridge high above them. The road curved left and then up a hill, half way up behind one of the stone walls was a police car. As he approached he notice the wooden gate that had been swung open to make access to the field that lead down to the lakes edge. He turned in.\nThere was a crowd already gathered down below around the lakes edge and the white tent that had been put around what he assumed was the body. He pulled to a stop next to the white and blue police car. Sam started to get out then hesitated, the music was now bubbling and he saw Inspector Watson didn't want move, let go by the sound of doom floating out clearly from all four corners of the car. Sam watched the face of his superior, the eyes were closed, his hands were off the stearing wheel and waving and wafting, creating clouds and creshendo's in time to the music. To oliver the picture formed as he closed his eyes of a dark cave with a storm flashing all around and a sweeping rain coming in. The darkness enveloping the clouds closing threateningly. \n“you coming?” broke the moment as sam poked his head back into the car. Slightly irritated his glance said it all and Sam moved out of the way of the storm clouds he felt coming and closed his door.\nOliver had now opened his eyes, he sat, his hands still, the real clouds over the peak had started covering the light for real and he watched the misty vapour coming, rolling down the side of the mountain threateningly. He knew how quickly the weather changed round here and a feeling of dissenchantedness came over him. He knew he had to leave the warm comfy seat that enclosed him, the music was now just that once again, just music. He pulled up his collar around his kneck and pulled on the door handle. With a gentle click the door slid open and the shock of the air outside rushed in with a gasp. He climbed out, looking down the hill as he closed the door. What sad social depravity awaited him down below he thought to himself, which of the many human emotions would be responsible, perhaps it was why he listened to the requiem, a preparation for looking death in the face, cold lifeless, an end. Sam was halfway down the bank now. The wind caught his collar and he dug deeper into his coat before he too started down.\nJust before he got to the bottom he felt the first drop of rain. He wasn't surprised, the clouds had been getting dark. Sam was waiting with a flap lifted up to the tent. He ducked and went in. The body was lying face down, the drag marks of his feet on the mud from the bank of the lake brought him his first question. “Hiya Quin” and he put his hand out. Quin, was dressed in white from head to foot, he was just peeling off his latex gloves and pulling off his mask. Taking olivers hand “still trolling the moors I see” he said with a smile. “Still trolling, ok then, what is this mess?”. Nothing to extraordinary for someone of your expertise, drowning, from the bang he took on the side of his head and the boat that was found drifting in the middle of the lake which we assume was his, it looks like he slipped and banged his head as he fell overboard. No ID is the main stumbling block!. I'll be able to confirm drowning when we get to the autopsy but my first opinion is death by missadventure”.\n“Ok” Oliver always got a little twinge in his kneck when called to a body, the twinge was gone and he relaxed, “just a matter of ID'ing the man then, could you turn him over so I can get a look at his face, might help”. Sam helped the other man dressed in white and they turned the body onto his back. Olivers eyes started at the feet, Smart shoes, trousers not jean, he remarked to himself “shoes not really made for this sort of terrain, trouser too don't really fit here, bit out of place here, I would assume visitor, not tourist because they are most of the time well equiped”. He stopped for a second as he perused the jacket worn. It was a heavy tweed coat, water was still running off from an edge but something had caught his attention sam though as he watched inspector Watsons face. It scrunched a bit, jaw lifted up and the wrinkles above his nose extenuated. Then suddenly the face cracked, suprise he assumed, he noticed the eyes were now focused on the corpses face. Did we get picture before searching for ID” he asked. “Of course”. “Can I take a look?” Oliver asked. Quin passed him the camera indicating where to press to move back and forth. His fat fingers caused him problems dealing with all this new technology, phones, computers, and cameras were the worst in his mind. He looked at the screen, there were close ups of the face, fingers and then he found what he was looking for, the body on his back in the grass. “Just to confirm, this was as he was found?” he passed the camera back to quin who looked. “Yep, as we found him” could you zoom in on the left pocket please” asked oliver. Quin pressed a few keys and handed back the camera. Oliver squinted and looked closely “hhmmm, Ok”, he looked up at quin “thanks, can you get me some prints of that”. He hesitated for a few seconds thinking,hand on his chin eyes to the ground searching, “are you going to do a detailed search of the immediate area?” Quin replied “not really planning to, the body was dragged out, anything that would have fallen from him would have gone in the water already. But if you want..........”, “hhhmmmm, nope, don't bother, cheers it's OK” and walked out of the tent.\nIt was now raining properly, as he tramped up the hill the path was starting to become just that in the middle of where that morning had been just green grass.\n\n\n\n\nFirst interview at hotel - Bar\n\nOliver turned to sam, "OK, you had better get back and send out the details for ?????, he can't get out of the country really but the sooner we find him the sooner we can clear him and let ???? know so she can stop worrying". \n"and you?". Oliver turned back and gave him a look, Sam shrunk a bit realising Oliver had something up his sleeve. "I'll call you later, perhaps in the morning. I just want to check out a few things" and carried on down the road in the direction of the shortcut they'd been pointed to in the pub.\nOliver climbed over the fence rather than take the extra fex meetres to the gate. He somehow wanted to prove to himself he wasn't the over 50 that he knew himself to be. he felt muscles he'd forgotten were there as he bent to get his foot on the other side and felt the awkward position he'd put himself in. 2 years ago he'd jump this fence as if it wasn't there but knew straight away, the 20 years that had passed had made a difference. Straihtening up, pushing past the ache that was suddenly there in his calf, he smiled to himself and walked on. the path lead past overgrown bushes that encroached on the path malking him duck from time to time. Obviously not used that often he noted. he finally came round a bend and the lake appeared. The path carried on following the bank of the river as far as he could see and he continued. Glancing across the lake to the bank on the other side he saw the white tent still there where they had been that morning. The sun was lowering and dusk wasnt far away. BY the side as he walked he saw swarms of midges hanging over the water, disturbing the flatness. There wasn't a breeze for the moment or he was in a place so protected the the gusts had no effect on the suface of the water.\nJust ahead he saw the end of a wooden pier. He assumed that was where the boats had been tied. He noted that he wanted to confirm that.\nHe got to the beginning of the pier and walked out to the end where he stopped and took in the size of the lake, the view and anything that might be of significance. noting the distance to where the body was dragged out, he made some rough assumptions. Turning to his left he saw the roof of the hotel and the group of pines that surrounded it. About 10 minutes walk he guessed following the assumed path with his minds eye.\nHe decided to wait till night fall, he wanted to see how dark it got, could you see from wherehe stood if someone was on the lake in the moonlight. He assumed not that much would have changed since the night before. He had a little idea forming in his head. HE started thinking about ????. She'd caught his attention and somehow, although he knew the odds to be so much agains it, he felt he'd seen her befre. The story was that she'd been in london about the time he'd been there as a cop. It wasn't impossible he told himself and as he waited for night to set in his mind wandered back in time. His old haunts, Cheshunt, Enfield Waltham cross. North London had been his ???????. \nHe'd lived in Hertford at the time. Down a little side street on the edge of town, Chambers street. It had been nice, a quiet sleepy town, little church at the end of the road, and occasionally, the white rover had come and picked him up. Back then he'd been in uniform.\nHe watched the sun tip the mountain to his left. Not long he thought to himself. he looked around, no moon yet though he could pick out the north star as the gloom was descending.\nHe started going through the pubs and clubs he'd frequented or been called out to more than once. The list was too long and he gave up quickly.\nHE stayed and eventually the sun dissapeared behind the crag. Darkness was upon him and still no moon. He could sense the water below with the occasional lap of water on the legs of the pier but as to being able to see anything on the lake....... His heart started to sink as not only his idea fell apart but he strted to realised that to follow the path in this blackness would be quite a job. "Fuck, you old fool" he said to himself with disgust and a touch of fear started to envelop him like that dakness that had now closed in leaving him blind. Hesitantly he picked himself up and got to his feet. Slidding his feet he followed his steps back along the pier. Then back off and he felt the soft wet mud under his shoes as he took to the shore again. He stopped for a minute to get his bearings. He saw a distant glow that he assumed was the hotel. Listening carefully he heard the lap of water against the shore line and slowly took his first step, followed by his second and so on. Feeling his way with the edge of his shoes he felt the dip of the path. It was slow going at first but determindly he continued. His courage built up and with it his speed until he jumped as a branch hit him scratching his cheek. cursing he wiped it. Automatically his hands came out in front of him now, he concentrated on the branches now he forgot about his feet and he realised his feet no longer felt the soft mud, it was different, slippery but different. He stopped and wondered if he should backtrack, find the path again as he felt he was no longer on it. He glanced up and saw the glow, though still a distance away, was a lot closer. Deciding to forget the path altogether, hands up, feeling, protecting his face he continued. The going was really slow though, he saw now the source of light that emitted the glow from before. A lamp above the entrance to the hotel. He was still a few hundred yards away. His spirits lifted and on he continued. A bit more sure footed, his pace increased until.....his right foot came down and there was nothin under neath, he continued lowering it, nothing there. He stoppped, but his back foot slipped a touch. Putting his right foot down instinctively where ground should be next to him, nothing there and he lost his balance as his left foot slipped again. reaching out with his hands for something to grab he felt a branch and clung on only for it to crack and then he toppled. His hand went out, down, to where the ground should be but nothing and then it all happened so quickly. He felt the water all around, panick hit him as he felt the void all around him and he struck out with all his limbs. A foot was the first to touch something and with every once of strength he centred on his toes, he pulled, his other foot came to solidish ground though soft and waving with his hands he managed to get some balance in a half swim. He knew he was floating or more half swimming. Realisaton that he was in the lake hit him and the cold spread ferociouscly through him as the water hit his skin under neath. His head that had been underwater for a second had broken to the surface now and he pushed on his feet, he felt them sink into silty mud and soon he was only waist deep, his arm out to his sides, water poured out of his jacket sleeves. Still recovering himself, he heard a voice. he couldn't make it out but he started shouting "over here, anyone there, help". He felt stupid the second it came out but he felt for real that for once he did need help. the voice came closer, he could make out it was female, he shouted again. HE saw the glow of a torch shaking towards him through the undergrowth, he shouted again "over here, i'm in the lake". He recognised the voice now. It was her, the manageress of the hotel. Pulling himself together and feeling the embarasement start, he put out his hands and started feeling for the bank. Hi felt some grass and grabbed with his hands, he started pulling his body forwards. It was then he realised as he tried to take a step forxwards that his foot was stuck in the mud. HE pulled carefully, trying to make sure the grass didn't give way in the effort. He felt the sucktion and pullng hard but evenly he felt the hold on his foot slowly give. The light was nearer now and he could see an outline now. With the foot he'd loosened from the mud he moved it forwards and searched for a ledge to get lift. He felt his naked foot on the cold mud now realising he'd lost his shoe in the process. cursing he realised there was nithing to be done about that and continued and tried reasuring his hand hold in vain till suddenly out of the black the light lit up his hnd and he saw another appear and take hold of one of his. he felt the pull added to his and again slowly felt the sucktion on his other foot. Curling his toes he was determind not to loose his other shoe. the effort was worth it and he felt the hold give and like a corck out of a bottle he was launched to the shore and landed flat on his stomach, one hand grabbing for grass to maintain his hold and the other still felt a pulling.\nHe looked up to see a concerned face looking down at him "INspector" was the gasp that came out. "What....come on, you'll catch your death out here". he stood up, she was still holding  his hand. He looked at her, she was looking him up and down now. He felt as if half the water from the lake was still in his pockets. Heavy, pullng him down.she gently pulled on his hand bringing him out of his daze, he followed, squelch, splash as alternately his shoed foot and socked foot, which he was suprised still held. Every part of him made a sound now as he followed like an embarassed school boy. \n\nShe took him in through the side entranc and told him to undress in the kitchen. She returned quickly with 2 large towels and turned her back as he tugged the sticking wet clothes off his skin till naked as he was born. He felt his cheeks warm like an embarrased boy he took the towel and wrapped it round himself. "You decent" she asked over her shoulder, "Decent as i can be" he attempted to sound as jovial as he could. She heard the shiver he tried to cover in his voice. She turned and wiht out thinking, putting her hands on his back started rubbing warmth back into him. He turned and looked. her eyes met his and for a second they locked, she quickly dropped he eyes and bent down to pick up his wet clothes. "Quickly, up through that door, left, through the next door and warm yourself by the fire. She picked up the still dripping clothes and dropped them in the sink. He followed her instructions and found himself in a small cosy room. THe ceiling was lower than in the rest of the hotel as far as he'd seen. there were nothing else in the room except for 2 old puffy armchairs placed facing the fire place. He felt unsure at first, it felt such a personal room. He didn't take a seat, but approached the fire and the warmth. He stayed stnding and turned his back to it. it felt homely, so unlike the image he'd had of her style he wondered....looking round the room he saw 2 paintings on opposite walls. The Faded colours gave him the feeling of age. The same Landscape he reckognised as being the craggs with the lake. one summery and bright, the other bleak in a way, giving off the power of nature. Opposite natures facing one another. He heard footsteps outside and felt himself stand a with bit more height.\nThe door opened. She walked in, a tray in one hand with glasses, over the other arm a set of clothes. "Roughly your size" and she placed them on the back of one of the armchair. I guess your a whiskey man, if not, tough" and she placed the glass in his hand the other she placed on the floor next to one of the armchairs. He nodded, she'd guessed right. \nTurning she left the room again. He took the time and climbed into the clothes. A bit tight round the edges, in length he had to fold over the sleeves and the legs. Realising it might be embarassing having to sit down in front of her he slowly eased himself into the other armchair trying not to bend too much with fear of hearing a split round his bum.\nOnce in he felt himself sink in. He sniffed the whiskey. Very peaty he thought, smokey, as he liked it. Very like the whiskeys he prefered from the isle of skye. He took a sip and felt the smoothness, the muscles in his back loosen as he savoured the flavour. His eyes closed, the crackle of the fire and the warm smooth liquid slipped down his throat. The cold of the lake dissapeared into a distant memory and he felt a lightness in his head.\nBrought back he heard the door open and she came in. "Talisker" he guessed and turned to see her smile and nod. She took her glass and eased herself into her chair as well. "Where is your assistant?", He felt the hardness had returned to her voice. "he went back to put out the search for your husband" he too took back his position as a cop. "So what are you still doing here, sneaking about at this time of night". "I wasn't sneaking....." the guilty child returned for a split second "we'll, ok it must have seemed like that but i made an error". She leaned forwards and looked at him. "You think it was something other than an accident don't you?!". \nHe looked at her ponderously, "OK, I wanted to get a feel for the place at night, you're right" he paused, " when sam asked you if you knew ???? before, you didn't want to answer, i have to confess, i did know him before" he studied her reaction which was blank. "I am guessing you did and in which case.......you know his crowd. I.....had a lot of dealings with them and one or 2 things lead me to believe there is something else going on, call it policmans intuition, it could be nothing but.....i hate leaving things hanging, i hate the grey" he took another gulp.\nShe stared at him, studying, trying to work out if she could trust him. All the hairs on her arms were bristling, she had learned never trust the bill, she had her reasons. she followed suit and took a big gulp. He was now watching her, the childishness had gone and back he was, being the cop, the one everyone hated, he'd learned to accept it, doing your job, upholding the law, ok he'd bent it a few times but only when necesarry he thought. Trying to keep people safe, and ?????? had been someone who had done people harm, he knew, he'd been on the end that picked up the pieces.\nhe looked at her and smiled, "they told me at the pub yur husband left there a bit the worse for wear at 2 o'clock in the morning. i wanted to see what he would see at night, lets say for instance, ???? for some strange reason was on the lake around that time, i wondered if your husband could catch a glimpse of ????? in his boat from the pier, so i waited till dark. unfortunately no moon, i got caught at the end of the pier and was left in the  dark.  i had to followed the light outside here, no moon, pitch black and a stupid old man falls in the lake only to be saved by the damsel in distress, ironic isn't it" and he let out an almost silent laugh to himself. He noticed she was staring, seriously and almost jumped as she cracked into a loud guphaw and threw up her arms. "you really are taking this seriously, my husband i mean?". He sat forward and turned to her with a serious face now. "If i may be honest, it's not your husbands involvement that has caught my attention, it is ???????. Your husband going missing is almost too much of a coincidence to me. Yes i am taking it seriously!!". "Sorry" she explianed, "i am a bit stressed and you taking me seriously seemed absurd, with a dead gangster on your plate......" she hesitated in contemplation, her face changed suddenly. "She looked up and at him, seriously "you don't think he's....ddead as well". Oliver quickly responded, "no i don't, the lake has been searched and no sign". She looked relieved he thought. He started wondering how far he could trust her, how much he could say. "Ehhhr, i understand you must be confused, so am i i have to admit. I can't work out why ????? was out on the lake at that time and have reason to believe, as much to his reputation, that it wasn't just to take in the air. Did you have any other clients or perhaps did you see anyone else around that might not have fitted in?". She looked at the fire place and stared for a short while, he waited, eventually she said "I have a confession to make, off the record, i don't want it to become gossip you know, its just that idid know ?????? from before, in fact he was a boyfriend of mine back then. I am guessing you'd find that out anyway. Well, last week, out of the blue i got a call, from ??????, he sounded stressed and asked if he could come up to see me, he said he had to get away for a while. I explained it wasn't the best of times as i knew it would cause problems between me and my husband as he is the really jealous type and i know ???? would wind him up but he insisted, i gave him the address and he turned up the next day. I told my husband about him and he went ballistic, he started drinking and dissapeared for a couple of days. So as you can see i wasn't to worried about him dissapearing till ?????'s body turned up and then i started jumping to silly conclusions but i guess if something happened........." she stopped as the penny dropped on what she was saying. "He's not a violent man, "he would't....". Oliver waited a moment, then leaning forward, "Did you get a chance to talk to ????? alone, you know, in private at anytime before". She looked at him suspiciously "what do you mean??". "I just want to ask you if he said anything about why he was here, what was he needing to hide from??". She hesitated and looked at Oliver. "He just said he'd got into trouble with ????????boss, he needed to keep his head low". \n"Ok, i don't think your husband had anything to do with the death, i think there was something he took, i have reason to believe someone took something from him just before, weather he was pushed or fell i don't know i just think there is something he brought from the south that caught up with him and that is what i'm curious to find out. What was that thing!!!". There was a moments pause "no, he didn't give me any idea though now you mention it, he stayed in his room a lot, and was suspicious of any other guest in the rooms near his. Now you come to mention it i would say that yes, it could be that he was trying to protect something in his room....But he did turn \n	0	t	2026-01-30 17:01:49.457	2026-01-30 17:01:49.457
cml14w8kk00077obqclpfk35e	cml14v4mh00067obqczgf6kyd	Chapter 1	Chapter 1 – Murder and kidnapping.\n\nWalking down the street just as dusk was setting. The street lights had just come on and the moths and mosquitos were already swirling round. It was early summer, Spring had been warm,  and the air already had its warm breezes.\nLucy turned to Charlotte and jabbed her in the ribs with her elbow. ‘What was that for?' she asked. with out opening her mouth Lucy pointed at Owen who was walking up ahead with Sebastian. ‘what…..what' she repeated with her hand covering her mouth. she didn't take her eyes off Owen but leaned in closer edging in her ear. waiting for a reply, she tripped and almost fell as she didn't notice the edge of the pavement. Catching herself in the stumble jarred her. ‘ooowww'. she uttered with a toothy sound as she felt the pang of pain from biting her tongue. Lucy who had been a pace behind burst into a laugh then in an instant she became more serious as she caught up with her sister. ‘you ok?'. Her sister nodded, her hand up to her cheek. ‘I it I tongue'. Owen had turned with Sebastian by this time looking back at the 2 girls. ‘come on, we want to get back for silent witness!!'. Charlotte had continued on with Lucy hunched over looking up at charlottes face, ‘show me', they reached the other side of the road by now and Charlotte stopped. her mouth hanging open she turned her tongue round in her mouth showing the side of her tongue that hurt. ‘an u thee anysing' she asked. Lucy stared up but in the light couldn't see anything, "can't see anything, tongue still there from what I see" hiding a giggle inside. Owen and Sebastian had turned round and come back. they too leaned over and looked up into charlottes mouth. after a couple of seconds, Sebastian said ‘what we looking for'. Lucy stepped back giving them both room to look, ‘she bit her tongue as she missed her step back there'.\n‘hhmmmpff' came from Owens' mouth, ‘tongues still there, should be more careful big feet' and then stepped back nervously joined Lucy. he turned his head towards Lucy. she stood gawping past Charlotte, eyes popping and she was pointing. Owen followed the stare and his jaw dropped giving the same gaze as Lucy. she had been staring up at the second-floor window. there was a curtain drawn but behind, a silhouette could be seen. a figure standing there, they could make out a head and shoulders they assumed with a thin horizontal shadow standing out from the person's chest.' someone just got stabbed' she uttered' in a sort of whisper' unknown to her Owen too was staring as the figure leaned and fell backwards disappearing from the window.\nLucy and Owen turned to each other, ‘did you see' Owen uttered flabbergasted. It was about this time Charlotte and Sebastian's eyes joined the same trajectory as Owen and Lucy's. ‘what….what!!' Charlotte uttered again.\nLucy's eyes were stuck now watching the rectangle of light that was the window upstairs. Owen opened his mouth, ‘i think…. I think she just saw' Lucy finished it off in a whisper ‘someone getting stabbed'. Sebastian the older of the 4 stood straight ‘yeh yeh' your just pulling our leg, how cou….' he stopped at that point as echoing through the silence a piercing wail started, coming from the same direction. "NNNOOOooooo". The wail reduced in volume till suddenly, it cut off.\nall 4 looked at each other, standing frozen, eyes popping out of their skulls, what seemed like seconds passed till Sebastian reacted first grabbing Lucy and Owen by their shoulders he dragged them in up the closest driveway. ‘shhh,' he whispered as the unavoidable crunch on the gravel broke through the now sudden silence that was enveloping them. Lucy scrambled past them and ducked crouching IN the big magnolia bush that leaned over the edge of the driveway. the others followed suit. Charlotte already had her phone out and was dialling 999. all of them looking up.\n\n"What have you done, we weren't here to kill him,